  "foaf:name": "Centre for Marine Restoration",
  "sdo:name": "Centre for Marine Restoration",
  "sdo:description": "The Center for Marine Restoration (SMR) is a major Bellona initiative addressing the collapse of 5,000 km² of kelp forest along Northern Norway’s coast, now replaced by sea urchin barrens due to past overfishing of predators such as cod and wolffish. This loss has reduced carbon storage, biodiversity, and annual fish stocks by around 50,000 tons. SMR will drive large-scale ecosystem recovery by coordinating research, technology, and documentation of restoration impacts. It will function as shared infrastructure for researchers, students, startups, volunteers, and industry, turning an ecological crisis into sustainable business and climate opportunities.",
